# Pairs with RAllOrNothing. The receiver ignores the stamped count and treats
# every terminal as final, which is the legacy behaviour applied to every
# saga: the registry is marked on the first source shard's terminal while
# another source shard's prepare has not yet arrived, and a receiver reader
# sees one key post-saga and the other pre-saga. The count-stamped tally is
# what holds the saga back until every source shard has reported.
MODULE: RAllOrNothingMarksOnFirstTerminal
TARGET: RAllOrNothing
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the receiver tally is final on the first terminal regardless of the stamped count
PERTURBS: DeliverTerminal

--- FIND
           final == legacy \/ Cardinality(arr2) >= exp2
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the tally completes on any arrival.
           final == TRUE
--- END
